# Line endings: LF in the index AND LF on checkout, for every text file.
#
# Why the explicit eol=lf: this machine's global Git config sets core.autocrlf=true
# (Git for Windows default), which made checkout hand back CRLF for every text file.
# That contradicted .editorconfig (`end_of_line = lf`) and made Git announce
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it" on every touched file,
# so ordinary edits churned line endings into unrelated diffs. A text attribute with
# an explicit eol wins over core.autocrlf, which makes the repo self-describing on
# any machine - Windows or Linux (the sound board targets both).
#
# The index is already all-LF, so this file changes checkout only: no history rewrite.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Real binary assets: never line-ending converted, never diffed as text.
# Of these, only .png is tracked today (265 sprite sheets); the rest guard assets
# that are expected to land here (fonts, audio, built .xnb) and any local-only ROM dump.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
*.mp3 binary
*.xnb binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
ref/rom/robotron64k.bin binary
